From 685389128540526b32242bae565bebd56569bc09 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 08:00:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] camera: copy raw frames on a recorder worker, not on
 libcamera's completion thread

The completion callback copied every 16.9 MB Clear HDR frame (plus the
12-bit code mapping) before giving the request back, on the same thread
that already spends ~15 ms per frame in libcamera's byte swap and stats.
The callback now hands the request to a copy worker that syncs the
dma-buf, copies into the page-aligned pool buffer, requeues the request
through a session callback and only then maps codes and queues the frame
for writing. At most buffers-2 requests are held so the CFE always has two
queued; a frame that finds no slot is counted (drop[copy-slot]) and its
request requeued at once. APERTAR_RAW_COPY_WORKERS (1-2) sizes the pool.
Not compiled here: build on the Pi.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01T93jucKMhWYnQM1yyFVkbH
